import SwiftUI
import KwipMLCore

enum TypedDecisionLessonContent {
 static let objective="This canvas learns how to route private support tickets. Read support tickets supplies text, a stable case_id and a label such as billing, technical or account. Partition keeps observations separate. Load model supplies Laya’s reviewed typed-decision encoder and head; Train updates their learned numbers. Decide uses the selected trained model to answer the same versioned question for held-out records.\n\nThis model selects declared options. It does not write chat responses. The small practice demonstrates the workflow, not reliable business accuracy."
 static let terms="- **Question set:** stable question keys, instructions and ordered option keys, saved as one immutable revision.\n- **State columns:** the record fields the model reads, not the answer labels.\n- **Head-only:** trains the decision head while the encoder stays fixed.\n- **Full:** trains both encoder and decision head.\n- **Review status:** whether independently fitted evidence supports accepting an answer. A high score alone is not a guarantee."
 static let steps=[
  "Select [Read support tickets](kwip-node://data/tickets). The bundled synthetic tickets have String columns case_id, text and label. You can replace them with your own CSV. Use unique case IDs and labels billing, technical or account. Keep repeated records from the same original source together; an arbitrary row split does not prevent semantic duplicates leaking across populations.",
  "Select [Load typed-decision model](kwip-node://control/decision-model). Review the pinned typed-decisions snapshot, its license and complete download inventory before Download & verify. A compatible local model folder also works. Only inert safetensors, reviewed ModernBERT configuration and its matching tokenizer are admitted; repository Python is never executed. This optional download is not part of first app installation.",
  "Select [Learn ticket decisions](kwip-node://control/train) and open Configure fine-tuning. Keep Typed decisions, state text, group case_id and category target label. Questions defines the allowed answers. Choose label targets or an explicit complete JSON probability distribution. Use qualified AdamW and CPU. Head-only changes the smaller decision head; full mode also updates the encoder. Validate & inspect checks real token budgets without training or silently truncating options. Apply the draft.",
  "Select [Save standalone decisions](kwip-node://control/save-model) and choose a new unused destination folder. Run Flow from Train. Inspect within-epoch loss and measured Validation through the standard Train results. Calibration is off for this small practice. Enabling it reserves independent Training groups before expansion and requires enough held-out support; Validation is never used to fit calibration. Insufficient support stops rather than manufacturing confidence.",
  "Open [Inspect decisions](kwip-node://data/decisions) and [Inspect every option](kwip-node://data/scores). Decide uses the saved model’s question revision and preserves one row per source/question plus every option probability in Scores. Confidence is the top option’s probability. Ordinal questions also report expected index; yes/no questions report true probability. Unqualified or unsupported policies remain marked for review. Double-click a long captured cell to inspect its bounded pages.",
  "Load the saved folder into a new Load model and connect it to Decide with the same input columns. Confirm matching probabilities. The package contains weights, matching tokenizer, questions and calibration provenance, without raw tickets. Continuing from these weights starts fresh optimizer memory. Evaluate uses an independent table without updates; repeated test exposure is recorded. Save your lesson project or Start fresh to keep an untouched practice."
 ]
 static let boundary="This editable practice is unscored. CPU ModernBERT typed-decisions, supervised head/full soft-target cross entropy. RLCD, Apple GPU, arbitrary architectures and exact optimizer/RNG resume are not enabled. Imported calibration is not a domain-quality promise. No clinical or security decision claims. Portable whole-flow Code refuses model-resource decisions explicitly; native Run Flow and Table Output retain standard outputs."
}
struct TypedDecisionLearningView:View {
 @ObservedObject var store:WorkspaceStore
 var body:some View {Button("Open typed-decision practice"){_=store.loadComponentWorkflowExample(TypedDecisionPracticeExample.exampleID,device:"cpu")}.buttonStyle(FlatButtonStyle()).disabled(store.isBusy)}
}
